idt-coordination
================

An exploration of how participants (people, agents, or both) come to know things together, and
of which ways of coordinating could work for one model or for many. It sits next to idt-swarm
(C:\IDT-Swarm), borrows from it, and is likely to be merged into it later.

It starts from the Atlas of Coordination and a reading of it as an epistemology, both kept in
source\. Neither is a standard to meet. Both are claims to try, and parts of either may be kept,
changed or dropped as runs show what works. The ledger is questioned first.


What is here
------------
  MAP           the typology made usable: four axes, nine types, their kin traditions, the
                smallest practice each implies, and the shadows, treated as hypotheses
  IMAGES        the typology read through images (rope, tree, ants, kintsugi…): an image for
                each type, candidate new types, and images still to look at
  CRITIQUE      parts of the Atlas and the reading under question, each with a verdict
                (keep, modify, set aside, discard, undecided), reasons and evidence
  CARRY-FORWARD what the runs suggest for a swarm made from a single model, and when not to
                swarm at all. Start here.
  COVENANT-DRAFT  a first covenant draft assembled from the runs; no field has consented to it
  PLAN          what to explore next, with estimated costs; no budget committed
  practices\    practices anyone can run, written in plain words for any model or person:
                  wonder          open a question up: I wonder, what if, let's try, then return
                  aggregate       read many partial views together, with no head-counting
                  consent-round   decide something that is safe enough to try
                  record-forms    the ways a run can remember: ledger, held, telling-only,
                                  layered
  runs\         one folder per run, holding what that run chose to keep; NOTES compares them
  source\       the Atlas, and the reading
  .claude\      the Claude Code side: one skill per practice, and running.md


Trying a practice
-----------------
In Claude Code, opened in this folder, ask for a practice by name ("run aggregate on …"), or
type /wonder, /aggregate or /consent-round.

The session proposes the run first: the question, who takes part and on which models, the record
form, and an estimate of cost. Your yes is needed for that and for anything that leaves this
folder. Nothing else waits on you. You can take part as a voice as much or as little as you like.

Without Claude Code, give any model (or any group of people) a PRACTICE.md and the record forms,
and the practice runs from the text alone.


Later, with idt-swarm
---------------------
  - Practices and record forms become options a field can choose, alongside idt-swarm's
    "Way:" line.
  - Records map to transcript entries, or replace them if CRITIQUE sets the ledger aside.
  - A covenant drafted here feeds idt-swarm's field covenant.
  - source\EPISTEMOLOGY.md links to an outside repository; review it before merging.
